            "typeName": "dsDescription",
            "multiple": true,
            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>This dataset consists of 3 shapefiles based on the COROP (i.e. NUTS3) zonation. Three non-overlapping zones for the Netherlands have been defined: Randstad, Intermediate Zone and Peripheral Zone. The definition of the zones follows from a publication by Wagtendonk, & Rietveld (2000) about spatial developments in the housing sector between 1980 and 1995.</p>"
                }
              },
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>The link between the zones and the underlying COROP/NUTS3-regions is maintained in the attribute table of the shapefiles. That way, you can see which COROP/NUTS3-regions are part of which zone (Randstad, Intermediate Zone, Peripheral Zone).</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
